DESCRIPTION:The Pikes Peak Marathon\, founded in 1956\, is the oldest continually held marathon in the United States. The Marathon takes runners from Manitou Springs to the summit of Pikes Peak at 14\,115 feet and back down for a total of 26.2 mountain miles. The sister race\, Pikes Peak Ascent\, climbs 13.3 miles up the historic Barr Trail to the summit. Both races climb approximately 7\,800 vertical feet.
