SUMMARY:Sangre de Cristo Trail Festival
DESCRIPTION:The 9th Annual Sangre de Cristo Trail Festival is a multi-distance trail and ultramarathon running event held on the Rainbow Trail in the Sangre de Cristo Mountains of Southern Colorado. Races range from 8 miles to 100 miles\, with start times varying by distance (100M/100K at 4:00 AM and 50M/50K at 6:00 AM on Saturday\, September 26; 27K/8-Mile at 8:00 AM on Sunday\, September 27). The event is based at Greenhorn/Music Meadows Ranch adjacent to the USFS Grape Creek Trailhead. Combined runner capacity is 350. Features include well-stocked aid stations\, finisher medals\, gender-specific race shirts\, camping\, and a strong community atmosphere. Online registration closes September 22\, 2026.
LOCATION:Greenhorn/Music Meadows Ranch\, County Road 119\, Westcliffe\, CO 81252
